            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Expanding adipose tissue in obesity requires a great deal of angiogenesis to support increasing volumes of tissue. A growing body of evidence indicates that inhibiting these blood vessels can result in substantial weight loss, and now this has been demonstrated in nonhuman primates.</AbstractText>
